      "worked": "Using the supplied identity,\n$$\\begin{align*}2(4\\cos^3\\theta-3\\cos\\theta)+1&=0\\\\2\\cos3\\theta+1&=0\\\\\\cos3\\theta&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=3\\theta$. Since $\\theta\\in[0,180^\\circ]$, $u\\in[0,540^\\circ]$. Cosine is negative in quadrants II and III, with related angle $60^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u&=120^\\circ,240^\\circ,480^\\circ\\\\3\\theta&=120^\\circ,240^\\circ,480^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=40^\\circ,80^\\circ,160^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
